<p>Russian missile and drone strikes killed at least 14 people across Ukraine on April 3, as Moscow launched a large daytime barrage that Ukrainian officials described as part of a shift in tactics in the more than four-year war. Ukrainian authorities said Russia used more than 500 drones and dozens of missiles. Damage was reported in the Kyiv region and in Sumy, Zhytomyr, Kharkiv, Donetsk, and Kherson regions, and officials introduced emergency power outages in several regions after the attacks. Officials and media reports said the recent pattern of daytime barrages may be meant to put more pressure on civilians and key infrastructure, while President Volodymyr Zelensky accused Russia of carrying out an &quot;Easter escalation&quot; ahead of upcoming holiday observances. At the same time, one analysis cited by Agence France-Presse said Russia&#x27;s territorial gains on the frontline slowed sharply in March to 23 square kilometers, the smallest monthly advance since September 2023. That suggests battlefield momentum has become more contested even as air attacks continue.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cPU1hDStU6CCAKnVQfHKz-APgP-NXruxk2HNRNFBo6PC0uAhj3j2dGbCVfG9pFuznC0ebgHh_g9P7wn6fl6231z1pAfmZkHD4xxN7xIH_3at_vA7NEk0n-993Ufx8Ojf4PewA3olp1bYWtoap4rQNEvLwS9owGB93TbiXRBofSXKoDDCosM1caV8KiTQDIAFFR8JrD7ewy0UcjOMs3pLSpPS7_DNYgznmI69H6CYT6Zy0ZRHqL5B5bCrCT445_L6jo14y5FhOg1sseStcQ' alt='An investigator collects debris from a Russian drone in a residential neighbourhood outside Kyiv, Ukraine, after a daytime strike on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Frontline slowdown: Agence France-Presse&#x27;s analysis of Institute for the Study of War data said Russian forces seized 23 sq km in March, down from 319 sq km in January and 123 sq km in February, while losing ground in some southern areas.</li><li>Civilian shelters: In Kyiv, some residents took shelter in the metro and in basements during air raid alerts, though Dawn reported that others stayed seated in cafes despite the sirens.</li><li>Animal losses: Kyiv regional governor Mykola Kalashnyk said about 20 animals died after the attack damaged a veterinary clinic in the capital region.</li><li>Local damage: In Zhytomyr region, one person was killed and 10 injured, while dozens of homes and public buildings were destroyed, according to Euronews&#x27; report from the area.</li></ul><blockquote>This is how Moscow responds to Ukraine’s Easter ceasefire proposals — with brutal attacks - Andriy Sybiga</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian government: President Volodymyr Zelensky said Russia was stepping up attacks before Easter and called the strikes an &quot;Easter escalation,&quot; while still signaling openness to a possible Easter truce. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3349002/8-die-ukraine-russian-strikes-kyiv-holds-door-open-easter-truce'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian foreign ministry: Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga cast the barrage as Moscow&#x27;s response to Ukraine&#x27;s ceasefire proposals, saying the attacks undercut prospects for a holiday pause in fighting. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988356/10-killed-as-russia-launches-daytime-attacks-on-ukraine'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Institute for the Study of War analysis via AFP: The analysis pointed to a steep drop in Russian territorial gains in March and linked the slowdown to localized Ukrainian counteroffensives, along with Russian restrictions affecting Starlink use and Telegram access. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/04/ukraine-war-briefing-russian-army-almost-no-territorial-gains-first-time-since-2023-analysis'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-14-people-killed-in-massive-russian-attack-on-1-500th-day-of-war/a-76652096'>Ukraine: 14 people killed in &#x27;massive&#x27; Russian attack on 1,500th day of war</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/04/ukraine-war-briefing-russian-army-almost-no-territorial-gains-first-time-since-2023-analysis'>Ukraine war briefing: Russian army records almost no territorial gains for first time since 2023, analysis shows</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3349002/8-die-ukraine-russian-strikes-kyiv-holds-door-open-easter-truce'>8 die in Ukraine in Russian strikes as Kyiv holds door open for Easter truce</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988356/10-killed-as-russia-launches-daytime-attacks-on-ukraine'>10 killed as Russia launches daytime attacks on Ukraine</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/14-dead-as-russia-launches-new-daytime-attacks-on-ukraine/article70821399.ece'>14 dead as Russia launches new daytime attacks on Ukraine</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/04/03/ukraines-zhytomyr-region-reels-after-missile-and-drone-strike'>Ukraine’s Zhytomyr region reels after missile and drone strike</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-ukraine-russia-zelensky-easter-escalation-strikes/'>Massive Russian daytime attack kills at least two people in Ukraine</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-8-as-kyiv-holds-door-open-for-easter-truce'>Russian strikes on Ukraine kill 8 as Kyiv holds door open for Easter truce</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/3/video-shows-the-moment-a-russian-drone-hit-an-apartment-in-ukraine'>Video shows the moment a Russian drone hit an apartment in Ukraine</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>